cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PaperForge in preparing academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "PaperForge: a chemistry manuscript engine with global research intelligence"
abstract: >-
  PaperForge composes, verifies, scores and packages chemistry manuscripts against 113
  machine-readable rules and 261 journal profiles, and provides a provider-based research
  intelligence layer that queries eleven open scholarly indexes (OpenAlex, Crossref,
  Europe PMC, arXiv, DataCite, DOAJ, Unpaywall, Semantic Scholar, ORCID, ROR, PubChem),
  normalises their records with explicit provenance, deduplicates them under an auditable
  rule set, and reports its own coverage gaps. It includes a preserved 1,616-work
  institutional dataset for the IISER Bhopal Department of Chemistry.
type: software
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
version: "2.4.0"
keywords:
  - chemistry
  - scholarly metadata
  - academic writing
  - openalex
  - crossref
  - bibliometrics
  - reproducibility
  - mass spectrometry
  - peer review
  - IISER Bhopal
